@nsobid-B39FEF373FB12154385D012AAB3BC99EF2944470

# Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream [010051F0207B2000] v1.0.4 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables every post-process anti-aliasing pass.
//
// All of the game's AA is agl::pfx::FilterAA, which dispatches on its
// antialias_type: 0 = FXAA (with history reprojection), 1 = ReduceAA, 2 = SMAA,
// 3 = a draw callback. Two renderers use it.
//
// The gsys final-image pass (sub_71001B2770) runs it when one test passes: the
// scene allows AA, the filter's scale is above zero, and the filter is enabled.
// A per-frame setup (sub_71001C3C64) repeats the test before it rewrites the
// filter's mode and scale. Both copies now take their false result, so the
// final image takes the engine's own no-AA route whatever the filter's
// parameters say.
//
// The snapshot renderer (sub_710058EEC8, whose targets are named SnapshotCmp,
// SnapshotPfx and SnapshotDepth) calls the filter directly and in place: the
// texture it samples is the color target it draws to. With AA off the filter
// would copy that texture onto itself, which emulators can show as flickering
// tiles. The call is removed instead, since the texture already holds the
// unfiltered image.

@enabled
001B27C4 2E000014   // B to the AA-off result in the final-image pass (was LDR S0,[X21,#0xC80] = FilterAA scale)
001C3CB8 03000014   // B to the return in the per-frame AA setup (was LDR S0,[X0,#0xC80])
005943D4 1F2003D5   // NOP (was BL sub_71021A3974 = snapshot FilterAA draw)
@stop

// Same agl/gsys FilterAA family as Splatoon 2; every site was derived in
// main.i64 for this build and byte-verified, not offset-guessed.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
